<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Command

Filters a list of commands as the user types, and moves a highlight through the matches with the arrow keys. Focus stays in the input, which points at the highlighted item with `aria-activedescendant`, so screen readers announce each item as the highlight moves. Enter or a click selects an item.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Command, CommandInput, CommandList, CommandEmpty, CommandGroup, CommandItem, CommandSeparator, CommandShortcut } from "#lib/components/ui/command/index.js";
	import { CalendarIcon, SmileIcon, CalculatorIcon, UserIcon, CreditCardIcon, SettingsIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<Command>
	<CommandInput placeholder="Type a command or search..." />
	<CommandList>
		<CommandEmpty>No results found.</CommandEmpty>
		<CommandGroup heading="Suggestions">
			<CommandItem><CalendarIcon />Calendar</CommandItem>
			<CommandItem><SmileIcon />Search Emoji</CommandItem>
			<CommandItem disabled><CalculatorIcon />Calculator</CommandItem>
		</CommandGroup>
		<CommandSeparator />
		<CommandGroup heading="Settings">
			<CommandItem><UserIcon />Profile<CommandShortcut>⌘P</CommandShortcut></CommandItem>
			<CommandItem><CreditCardIcon />Billing<CommandShortcut>⌘B</CommandShortcut></CommandItem>
			<CommandItem><SettingsIcon />Settings<CommandShortcut>⌘S</CommandShortcut></CommandItem>
		</CommandGroup>
	</CommandList>
</Command>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/command.json
```

## Anatomy

`Command` holds the search and the highlight, and handles the arrow, Home, End, and Enter keys. `CommandInput` filters the items, and `CommandList` scrolls once it passes `300px`. Inside the list, `CommandGroup` takes a `heading` and hides itself while none of its items match.

`CommandItem` is the selectable row. `CommandShortcut` shows a key hint at the end of an item and is left out of its search text. `CommandSeparator` divides groups and hides while searching. `CommandEmpty` shows only while no item matches, so place it inside `CommandList`.

## Dialog

`CommandDialog` renders a `Command` in a modal `Dialog` and takes every `Command` prop. Use `bind:open` to open it from a button or a keyboard shortcut. Opening it focuses the input, and Escape or a click on the backdrop closes it. Set `title` to name the dialog for assistive technology; it defaults to `"Command menu"`.

<Demo section="dialog" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { CommandDialog, CommandInput, CommandList, CommandEmpty, CommandGroup, CommandItem } from "#lib/components/ui/command/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";

	let isOpen = $state(false);

	/** Toggles the menu with Cmd+K or Ctrl+K. */
	const handleShortcut = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
		if (e.key !== "k" || !(e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey)) return;
		e.preventDefault();
		isOpen = !isOpen;
	};
</script>

<svelte:window onkeydown={handleShortcut} />

<Button variant="outline" onclick={() => (isOpen = true)}>Open command menu</Button>

<CommandDialog bind:open={isOpen}>
	<CommandInput placeholder="Type a command or search..." />
	<CommandList>
		<CommandEmpty>No results found.</CommandEmpty>
		<CommandGroup heading="Suggestions">
			<CommandItem onSelect={() => (isOpen = false)}>Calendar</CommandItem>
			<CommandItem onSelect={() => (isOpen = false)}>Search Emoji</CommandItem>
		</CommandGroup>
	</CommandList>
</CommandDialog>
```

The dialog stays open after a selection, so close it in `onSelect` when the command is done.

## Filtering

An item matches when every word of the search appears in its text, `value`, or `keywords`, ignoring case. Add `keywords` to match synonyms that are not shown, such as `theme` for a dark mode item.

<Demo section="filtering" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<CommandItem keywords={["theme", "night"]}>Dark mode</CommandItem>
```

Pass `filter` to replace the matching. It receives the item's text, value, and keywords joined by spaces, plus the search, and returns whether the item matches. Set `shouldFilter={false}` to show every item and filter them yourself, such as with results loaded from a server.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Command filter={(text, search) => text.toLowerCase().startsWith(search.toLowerCase())}>
	<CommandInput />
	<CommandList>...</CommandList>
</Command>
```

## Controlled

Use `bind:search` to read or set the input text, and `bind:value` to read or set the highlighted item. `onSelect` on an item receives its `value`, which defaults to the item's text. Set `loop` to wrap the arrow keys between the first and last items.

<Demo section="controlled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Command, CommandInput, CommandList, CommandEmpty, CommandGroup, CommandItem } from "#lib/components/ui/command/index.js";

	let search = $state("");
	let selected = $state("");
</script>

<Command bind:search>
	<CommandInput placeholder="Search..." />
	<CommandList>
		<CommandEmpty>No results for "{search}".</CommandEmpty>
		<CommandGroup heading="Pages">
			<CommandItem value="home" onSelect={(value) => (selected = value)}>Home</CommandItem>
			<CommandItem value="docs" onSelect={(value) => (selected = value)}>Documentation</CommandItem>
		</CommandGroup>
	</CommandList>
</Command>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` on `Command` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg` to change the input height, item padding, icons, and text. The default is `md`, and the corner radius follows the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Command size="lg">
	<CommandInput />
	<CommandList>...</CommandList>
</Command>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` on `Command` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius. Items use one step smaller so the corners nest. `pill` is a true pill and can clip tall content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round corners that stay safe.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Command rounded="lg">
	<CommandInput />
	<CommandList>...</CommandList>
</Command>
```

## Overrides

`CommandItem` takes `rounded` to set that item's exact radius over the list's item radius.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<CommandItem rounded="pill">Calendar</CommandItem>
```

## API

`Command`, `CommandList`, `CommandEmpty`, `CommandGroup`, `CommandItem`, and `CommandSeparator` extend the native `div` attributes, and `CommandShortcut` extends `span`. `CommandInput` passes extra attributes such as `placeholder` to the `input`, and merges `class` onto its wrapper. Highlighted items set `data-selected` for custom styles.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Value of the highlighted item; supports `bind:value` */
	value?: string;
	/** Called with the new value when the highlight moves */
	onValueChange?: (value: string) => void;
	/** Text in `CommandInput`; supports `bind:search` */
	search?: string;
	/** Called with the new text as the user types */
	onSearchChange?: (search: string) => void;
	/** Hides items that do not match the search; set `false` to filter the items yourself; defaults to `true` */
	shouldFilter?: boolean;
	/** Decides whether an item matches; receives the item's text, value, and keywords joined by spaces */
	filter?: (text: string, search: string) => boolean;
	/** Wraps the arrow keys between the first and last items; defaults to `false` */
	loop?: boolean;
	/** Input height, item padding, and text on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of the root and items; follows `size` when omitted. `pill` makes the panels pills too, which can clip their items, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round panels */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface DialogProps extends Props {
	/** Whether the dialog is shown; supports `bind:open` */
	open?: boolean;
	/** Accessible name of the dialog; defaults to `"Command menu"` */
	title?: string;
}

interface GroupProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Muted heading above the items; also names the group */
	heading?: string;
}

interface ItemProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Value reported to `onSelect` and the root `value`; defaults to the item's text */
	value?: string;
	/** Extra words that also match the item, such as synonyms */
	keywords?: string[];
	/** Blocks selecting the item; the arrow keys skip it */
	disabled?: boolean;
	/** Called with the item's value when it is clicked or chosen with Enter */
	onSelect?: (value: string) => void;
	/** Corner radius of this item with this exact value; overrides the list's item radius */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
